rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: A Makefile that builds instead of testing is production evidence, refused for a weakened assertion (D-199)
d199: D-199 (0.12) refuses repair evidence for this rule. The inputs are unchanged; they were the case runner_build_makefile_neg, held at warn by that evidence. REPAIR_EVIDENCE_REFUSED pins that the production change still reached the finding.
origin: FP guard for the 2026-08-11 runner widening — filename must not decide this, content must
=== before: Makefile ===
libfast.so: fast.c
	$(CC) -O2 -shared -o libfast.so fast.c
=== after: Makefile ===
libfast.so: fast.c
	$(CC) -O3 -shared -fPIC -o libfast.so fast.c
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) > 0
